{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Therefore</b> — The view of many commentators: that it means prepare yourself to return to HaShem. In my view: it is like the pattern of 'come to Bethel.' The meaning: I have brought evil upon evil upon you, and now prepare yourself and get ready to go out to meet your Elohim for battle. And the meaning of 'your Elohim' is 'to meet Me,' for you regarded Me as your Elohim; therefore it follows it."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:03.008045188Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}